          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The usual answer has three parts, and they all run inside the cluster."
        },
        {
          "text": "First, an agent on every node. It runs as a DaemonSet, a workload that puts exactly one pod on each node."
        },
        {
          "text": "It tails those files, labels each line with its namespace, pod and container, and ships it off the node."
        },
        {
          "text": "We use Grafana Alloy. Promtail did this job until it reached end of life in March 2026, and Fluent Bit is the other common choice.",
          "senses": {
            "use": "verb"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Second, a store: Grafana Loki, as one pod, with its data on a PersistentVolume and a retention period of 14 days."
        },
        {
          "text": "Third, Grafana, to search it all, including pods that no longer exist."
        },
        {
          "text": "Many companies also forward logs to a system they already run, and the agent can send to both.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
